-- title:
--   Abel–Jacobi: Pic⁰ of a complex function field is ℂ^g/L
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field equipped with an algebra structure over $\mathbb{C}$, and assume $F$ is a function field in one variable over $\mathbb{C}$ in the sense that some $x \in F$ is transcendental over $\mathbb{C}$ and $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $\mathbb{C}(x)$ generated by $x$. Assume further that $F$ is a curve over $\mathbb{C}$, i.e. every nonzero $f \in F$ has a finitely supported divisor whose value at each place $v$ is $v.\mathrm{ord}\,f$ and whose degree is $0$, every place has residue field finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{C}$, and $\Omega_{F/\mathbb{C}}$ is free of rank one over $F$; here a place is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $\mathbb{C}$, distinct from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring. Assume also that canonical divisors exist: every nonzero $\omega \in \Omega_{F/\mathbb{C}}$ has a finitely supported divisor whose value at each place $v$ is $v.\mathrm{ordDifferential}\,\omega$. Write $g = \mathrm{genus}\,\mathbb{C}\,F$, defined as $(\deg K + 2)/2$ (truncated to $\mathbb{N}$) for the canonical divisor $K$ attached to a chosen nonzero differential, and $0$ if $\Omega_{F/\mathbb{C}} = 0$. Then there is a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $L$ of $\mathbb{C}^g$ (functions $\mathrm{Fin}\,g \to \mathbb{C}$) which is free and finite over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\mathrm{finrank}_{\mathbb{Z}} L = 2g$, together with an isomorphism of additive groups between $\mathrm{Pic}^0(F/\mathbb{C})$ — the group of degree-zero divisors modulo the subgroup of principal divisors contained in it — and $\mathbb{C}^g/L$.
--
--   This is the Abel–Jacobi and Jacobi inversion theorem in the form 'the degree-zero divisor class group of a compact Riemann surface of genus $g$ is a complex torus $\mathbb{C}^g/L$ with period lattice of rank $2g$', stated for the function field of the curve. It is used to compute the $p$-torsion of $\mathrm{Pic}^0$, namely in [`AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.natCard_torsion_prime_eq_pow_genus_complex`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.natCard_torsion_prime_eq_pow_genus_complex).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Pic0_exists_addEquiv_quotient_submodule_complex.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_CanonicalDivisor

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open AlgebraicCurve

theorem AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.exists_addEquiv_quotient_submodule_complex
    (F : Type*) [Field F] [Algebra ℂ F]
    (hfg : ∃ x : F, Transcendental ℂ x ∧
      FiniteDimensional (IntermediateField.adjoin ℂ ({x} : Set F)) F)
    [IsCurveOver ℂ F] [HasCanonicalDivisor (K := ℂ) (F := F)] :
    ∃ (L : Submodule ℤ (Fin (genus ℂ F) → ℂ)),
      Module.Free ℤ L ∧ Module.Finite ℤ L ∧
      Module.finrank ℤ L = 2 * genus ℂ F ∧
      Nonempty (Pic0 ℂ F ≃+ (Fin (genus ℂ F) → ℂ) ⧸ L) := by sorry
